                <pb facs="0335" n="275" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg275"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Eustis to Mr. Adee</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-08-19"><hi rendition="#italic">August 19,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The evidence has never been received in Paris. Expected at the end of this month.
                    In the absence of minister for foreign affairs, I have received confidential
                    assurance from the foreign office by the official in charge of the matter that
                    when received the evidence will be communicated to me. Access Waller
                    accorded.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eustis</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
